From 8ee2a3326d03e6f24d89fb78ea09fe04f90a1479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emil Boenke <boenkeemil@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:22:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] German spelling: compounds, de-AT, and the system language as
 default
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

German dictionaries build words by compounding through affix continuation
classes, which the spell checker didn't read, so most German text was
flagged; new text was always checked as US English.

- spell: Hunspell compounding as the igerman98 dictionaries use it (compound
  flags on roots or continuation classes, COMPOUNDPERMITFLAG,
  COMPOUNDFORBIDFLAG, ONLYINCOMPOUND, COMPOUNDFIRST), CIRCUMFIX, CHECKSHARPS,
  MAP groups as REP pairs; suffix rules indexed by appended text.
- suggestions: capitalized candidates for nouns (Kaffeclub -> Kaffeeclub,
  haustür -> Haustür); TRY capitals skipped for lower-case candidates.
- dictionaries: LibreOffice `*_frami` names for the exact region, LibreOffice
  extension folders, LOCALAPPDATA, and a `dictionaries` folder beside the program.
- text without a language is checked in the system's language (de-AT on an
  Austrian Windows; DECKCRAFT_LANG overrides), not always en-US.
- single letters of hyphenated words (E-Mail) aren't flagged; Deutsch
  (Österreich) in Review > Language.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
