 //! A subset of Hunspell: `SET` (UTF-8 and ISO-8859-1), `FLAG` (default, `long`, `num`, `UTF-8`),
 //! `PFX`/`SFX` with strip, conditions and cross products, continuation flags on affixes (one
 //! level: a suffix that allows a further suffix), `NEEDAFFIX`, `FORBIDDENWORD`, `NOSUGGEST`,
-//! `KEEPCASE`, `TRY`, `REP` and `WORDCHARS`. Compounding, `ICONV`/`OCONV` and morphology are not
-//! read; words they would accept are reported as misspelt.
+//! `KEEPCASE`, `CIRCUMFIX`, `CHECKSHARPS`, `TRY`, `REP`, `MAP` (multi-letter items such as
+//! `(ss)ß` become REP pairs) and `WORDCHARS`.
+//!
+//! Compounding as German dictionaries use it: `COMPOUNDFLAG`, `COMPOUNDBEGIN`/`MIDDLE`/`END`
+//! (`FIRST`/`LAST`), `COMPOUNDPERMITFLAG`, `COMPOUNDFORBIDFLAG`, `ONLYINCOMPOUND`, `COMPOUNDMIN`
+//! and `COMPOUNDWORDMAX`. The compound flags may sit on a root or on an affix's continuation
+//! classes (`SFX j 0 0/xoc`: `Kaffee` as a first part); suffixes inside a compound and prefixes on
+//! its last part need the permit flag, as in Hunspell. `COMPOUNDRULE`, `ICONV`/`OCONV` and
+//! morphology are not read; words they would accept are reported as misspelt.
 //!
 //! No dictionary ships with DeckCraft. They are looked up in the folders the system's own spell
 //! checkers use (and `DECKCRAFT_DICTIONARIES`), so whatever the user installed is used.
